; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Bounce
; CATEGORY: Classic Logo
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     animation, reflection, headings, sound
; SUMMARY:  A turtle ball bounces around a billiard table, beeping at each cushion and leaving a colorful trail.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   The turtle runs around inside a table. When it reaches a side it
;   bounces off like a billiard ball, changes the color of its trail and
;   beeps. After a while the trail makes a criss-cross lattice.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run and watch (turn the sound on). Press Stop to end it.
;   Change the starting heading at the bottom, for example to 30 or 45.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * how a heading changes when something bounces off a wall
;   * IF to check the walls on every step
;   * a simple animation loop with WAIT
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Start with heading 45 on a square table. What happens?
;   * Make the table smaller or wider.
;   * Add a second turtle with a different heading.
; ============================================================

; Bouncing things were one of the first animations people wrote in Logo.
; The geometry is simple and worth knowing. A heading counts clockwise
; from straight up. Bouncing off a left or right wall flips the
; sideways part of the motion, which makes the new heading 360 minus
; the old one. Bouncing off the top or bottom flips the up-down part:
; the new heading is 180 minus the old one.

make "halfwidth 330
make "halfheight 220

to table
  penup setxy 0 - :halfwidth - 12 0 - :halfheight - 12 setheading 0 pendown
  setpencolor [90 50 20]
  setpensize 16
  repeat 2 [forward 2 * :halfheight + 24 right 90 forward 2 * :halfwidth + 24 right 90]
  setpensize 2
end

to beep
  tone 300 + random 500 25
end

to next.color
  make "hue :hue + 1
  setpencolor item 1 + remainder :hue 6 [[255 220 80] [255 120 120] [120 220 255] [200 160 255] [140 255 160] [255 180 90]]
end

; One step of the ball. After moving, check each wall. We also put the
; ball back inside the wall, so it can never get stuck outside.
to move.ball
  forward 6
  if (abs xcor) > :halfwidth [
    setheading 360 - heading
    setx :halfwidth * sign xcor
    next.color beep
  ]
  if (abs ycor) > :halfheight [
    setheading 180 - heading
    sety :halfheight * sign ycor
    next.color beep
  ]
end

to sign :n
  if :n < 0 [output -1]
  output 1
end

to bounce :start.heading
  clearscreen
  setbackground [20 90 50]
  table
  make "hue 0
  penup home pendown
  setheading :start.heading
  setshape "circle
  showturtle
  next.color
  repeat 3000 [
    move.ball
    if (remainder repcount 4) = 0 [wait 1]
  ]
end

bounce 23
